---
title: Client Persistence
id: client-persistence
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":" (and every framework "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat"},{"type":"text","value":") keeps messages in\nmemory, so a reload or a crashed tab loses the whole conversation and any reply\nthat was still streaming. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" option fixes that from the browser\nside: on reload it repaints the transcript, brings back a pending interrupt, and\nrejoins a run that was mid-stream."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You need this whether or not you have a server:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The browser owns the chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (SPA, offline-first, no server store). Pass a\nstorage adapter and it holds the full transcript, restored on reload with no\nnetwork."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server owns the chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (you use "},{"type":"link","href":"./chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":").\nSet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":" and the client caches nothing: on reload it hydrates\nthe thread from the server by its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", painting the conversation and\nrejoining any run still streaming. That is the server-authoritative mode below."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"turn-it-on","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turn it on"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a storage adapter as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" and give the chat a stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" so\na reload finds the same record:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  localStoragePersistence,\n  useChat,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n  })\n  // ...render messages, call sendMessage(text)\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localStoragePersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" needs no type argument and no codec: it defaults to\nthe chat record shape and a JSON codec. That is the whole opt-in."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" is doing the real work here: it is the key the record is written\nunder and looked up by, so a fresh id per mount restores nothing. Derive it from\nyour own domain (a conversation id, a route param). "},{"type":"link","href":"./id-map","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Id map"}]},{"type":"text","value":" covers how\nto pick one and how it differs from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" the hook reports."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-a-reload-restores","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a reload restores"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client stores one record per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", the transcript plus a small resume\npointer. On the next load "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" reads it and:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repaints the transcript"}]},{"type":"text","value":" from storage with no network. Sync adapters\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionStorage"},{"type":"text","value":") hydrate during construction. IndexedDB\nhydrates asynchronously after the database opens. Until then, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isHydrating"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", so you can show a loading state instead of an empty chat."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rehydrates a pending interrupt"}]},{"type":"text","value":", so an approval prompt comes back exactly as\nit was."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejoins an in-flight run"}]},{"type":"text","value":", if a reply was still streaming when the page\nreloaded, so it finishes in place instead of freezing half-done. This one needs\na durability-backed connection (a route that records the stream and exposes a\nreplay handler); see "},{"type":"link","href":"../resumable-streams/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable streams"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replay rebuilds reasoning, tool activity, and text from the durable log, including runs that emit reasoning before their first tool or text event. The completed activity remains in the transcript sent with the next message."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ag-ui-activity-rows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI activity rows"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI activity events show as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'activity'"},{"type":"text","value":" rows in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A client storage adapter keeps each row with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" and content."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":" restores the rows from the server only when the server\nhas an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activities"},{"type":"text","value":" store. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./chat-persistence#ag-ui-activity-rows-on-reload","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI activity rows on reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":" does not send activity rows as model input."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"handle-restored-client-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle restored client tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A live client tool runs automatically when its call arrives from the stream.\nHydration restores its pending execution but does not run the browser code\nagain, because that work may not be safe to repeat. The execution remains an\ninternal interrupt and does not appear in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptStateChange"},{"type":"text","value":" to distinguish restored interrupt state from live\nupdates. Leaving a restored batch pending is the default. This example cancels\nevery restored batch instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  localStoragePersistence,\n  useChat,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const [restoredBatch, setRestoredBatch] = useState(false)\n  const { cancelInterrupts } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n    onInterruptStateChange(_state, { source }) {\n      setRestoredBatch(source === 'hydrate')\n    },\n  })\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (restoredBatch) cancelInterrupts()\n  }, [cancelInterrupts, restoredBatch])\n\n  return null\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" for state restored from an initial resume snapshot, a\nclient storage adapter, or server hydration. It is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live"},{"type":"text","value":" for streamed and\nclient-initiated changes. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelInterrupts()"},{"type":"text","value":" cancels the complete internal\nbatch, including visible approvals and hidden client-tool executions; it does\nnot selectively cancel one kind of interrupt."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-a-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a mode"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" takes a storage adapter or a boolean:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: localStoragePersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":") is client-authoritative."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is server-authoritative."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (or omitted) is off: messages live in memory only and a reload starts empty."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The generation hooks take the same option, boolean only. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generation-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"an-adapter-client-authoritative","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An adapter: client-authoritative"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the adapter directly, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: localStoragePersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":". The\ntranscript and the resume pointer both live in the browser. The client owns the\nhistory; the server, if any, mirrors it. Best when the browser is the source of\ntruth: single-page apps, offline-first, one device, small to moderate\nconversations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"true-server-authoritative","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":": server-authoritative"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":". The client stores nothing, no transcript and no resume\npointer. On mount "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" hydrates the thread from the server by its\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":": it paints the stored transcript and, if a run is still generating,\ntails it to completion. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"history: { pageSize }"},{"type":"text","value":" paints the newest window on\nhydrate. Best when transcripts are large (localStorage is\nsynchronous and quota-bound), when the same conversation must open on another\ndevice, or when you simply do not want message content in the browser."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not fetch or seed the transcript yourself. A reload and the same thread\nopened on another device follow the identical path, because the thread id is the\nstable key and the server resolves everything from it. No loader, no\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialMessages"},{"type":"text","value":", no extra props. It needs a connection with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" handler\n(every built-in connection has one) and the server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" endpoint below."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"text","value":": a connection, a stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nfunction Chat({ threadId }: { threadId: string }) {\n  const {\n    messages,\n    isHydrating,\n    hasOlderMessages,\n    loadOlderMessages,\n    sendMessage,\n  } = useChat({\n    threadId,\n    connection,\n    persistence: true,\n    history: { pageSize: 50 },\n  })\n  if (isHydrating) return <p>Loading conversation...</p>\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {hasOlderMessages ? (\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          onClick={() => {\n            void loadOlderMessages().catch(() => {\n              // Show a retry. Painted messages stay.\n            })\n          }}\n        >\n          Load older\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      {messages.map((m) => (\n        <div key={m.id}>{m.role}</div>\n      ))}\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => void sendMessage('hi')}>\n        Send\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadOlderMessages()"},{"type":"text","value":" from your scroll handler. The library does not watch\nthe scrollbar."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isHydrating"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" from the first render until the transcript is in\nplace. If a run is still generating, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":" is already "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isHydrating"},{"type":"text","value":" turns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":". If the load fails, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isHydrating"},{"type":"text","value":" turns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" is set."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasOlderMessages"},{"type":"text","value":" follows "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"page.truncated"},{"type":"text","value":" on the last hydrate or older-page\nresponse."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"history"},{"type":"text","value":", hydrate loads the full thread."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"history"},{"type":"text","value":" is only valid with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"history.pageSize"},{"type":"text","value":", send posts only the new turn. Reload posts the last\nuser (the old assistant is already gone locally). Resume posts from that\nuser through the painted assistant so the stored tool-call is not dropped."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadOlderMessages()"},{"type":"text","value":" fails, the promise rejects and painted messages\nstay. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasOlderMessages"},{"type":"text","value":" stays true. Catch the rejection in your UI."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server"}]},{"type":"text","value":": one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" endpoint next to your chat "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"POST"},{"type":"text","value":". Replay the durability\nlog when the request carries a resume cursor, otherwise return the stored\nconversation with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { memoryStream, resumeServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Response | Promise<Response> {\n  const durability = memoryStream(request)\n  // A reconnecting client carries a resume cursor (Last-Event-ID / ?offset and\n  // X-Run-Id / ?runId). Replay the log so the run finishes in place.\n  if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n    return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n  }\n  // Otherwise return the stored transcript plus a cursor to any in-flight run.\n  // Guard access in multi-user apps (see authorize in Chat persistence).\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ messages, activeRun }"},{"type":"text","value":": the transcript as UI\nmessages, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":" when a run is still generating for the thread. With a\nvalid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"limit"},{"type":"text","value":" query param, the body also has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"page: { truncated, cursor }"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"limit"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before"},{"type":"text","value":" from the query."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client calls this endpoint on mount and, when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":" is set, tails the\nrun through the replay branch above. You never handle a run id, and a second\ndevice resumes the live run the same way the original tab does. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"show-how-long-each-turn-took","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show how long each turn took"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A live turn can time itself on the client. After a reload, that time is gone. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeRuns: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to get it back from the server:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request, { includeRuns: true })\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each assistant message of a finished run then has the run's timings, in epoch ms, on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.run"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { UIMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction TurnDuration({ message }: { message: UIMessage }) {\n  const run = message.metadata?.tanstack?.run\n  if (!run?.finishedAt) return null\n  const seconds = Math.round((run.finishedAt - run.startedAt) / 1000)\n  return <span>Worked for {seconds}s</span>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The response also has a top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" list with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startedAt"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishedAt"},{"type":"text","value":" for each finished run. The timings need a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" store that implements "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByThread"},{"type":"text","value":", and messages that were saved by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" with this version or later."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caches on client"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authoritative history"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reach for it when"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: store"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"transcript + resume pointer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SPA / offline, one device, small to moderate history"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nothing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"large histories, multi-device, no transcripts in the browser"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-a-storage-backend","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a storage backend"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three adapters ship from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":", re-exported from every framework\npackage. All share the same shape; they differ in lifetime and encoding."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifetime"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reach for it when"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localStoragePersistence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"across reloads and browser restarts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"synchronous, ~5MB quota, JSON codec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the default: persist a conversation for next time"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionStoragePersistence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"one tab, cleared when it closes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same shape as localStorage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a conversation that should not outlive the tab"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"indexedDBPersistence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"across reloads and restarts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async, structured clone (a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date"},{"type":"text","value":" round-trips exactly), room for large data"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"big transcripts, or values a JSON codec would mangle"}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { indexedDBPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst persistence = indexedDBPersistence()","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each throws only lazily, per operation, when its backing store is missing (for\nexample during server-side rendering), so constructing one on the server is safe."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"writing-your-own","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writing your own"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Any object with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getItem"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setItem"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"removeItem"},{"type":"text","value":" works. The record is one\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ messages, resume? }"},{"type":"text","value":" blob per chat id (the transcript plus the pointer that\nlets a reload rejoin an in-flight run), so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setItem"},{"type":"text","value":" receives that whole record,\nnot a bare message array:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type {\n  ChatClientPersistence,\n  ChatPersistedState,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nfunction isPersistedState(value: unknown): value is ChatPersistedState {\n  return (\n    typeof value === 'object' &&\n    value !== null &&\n    'messages' in value &&\n    Array.isArray(value.messages)\n  )\n}\n\nconst persistence: ChatClientPersistence = {\n  getItem(id) {\n    const raw = localStorage.getItem(id)\n    if (raw === null) return null\n    const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(raw)\n    // A bare array is the legacy messages-only format, still accepted.\n    if (Array.isArray(parsed)) return { messages: parsed }\n    return isPersistedState(parsed) ? parsed : null\n  },\n  setItem(id, state) {\n    localStorage.setItem(id, JSON.stringify(state))\n  },\n  removeItem(id) {\n    localStorage.removeItem(id)\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads are best-effort: a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getItem"},{"type":"text","value":" that throws or returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" is treated as\n\"nothing stored\", so an adapter that parses the wrong shape fails "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"silently"}]},{"type":"text","value":":\nthe conversation just does not come back. Round-trip your adapter once against a\nreal reload before shipping it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-and-server-are-independent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client and server are independent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client persistence restores what one browser rendered. Server persistence\n("},{"type":"link","href":"./chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":") keeps the authoritative copy for every\nuser and survives a server restart. They compose: for the combination we\nrecommend for most apps, and why, see the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./overview#what-we-recommend","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"turn-it-on","text":"Turn it on","level":2},{"id":"what-a-reload-restores","text":"What a reload restores","level":2},{"id":"ag-ui-activity-rows","text":"AG-UI activity rows","level":3},{"id":"handle-restored-client-tools","text":"Handle restored client tools","level":3},{"id":"choose-a-mode","text":"Choose a mode","level":2},{"id":"an-adapter-client-authoritative","text":"An adapter: client-authoritative","level":3},{"id":"true-server-authoritative","text":"true: server-authoritative","level":3},{"id":"show-how-long-each-turn-took","text":"Show how long each turn took","level":3},{"id":"choose-a-storage-backend","text":"Choose a storage backend","level":2},{"id":"writing-your-own","text":"Writing your own","level":3},{"id":"client-and-server-are-independent","text":"Client and server are independent","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA `ChatClient` (and every framework `useChat` / `createChat`) keeps messages in\nmemory, so a reload or a crashed tab loses the whole conversation and any reply\nthat was still streaming. The `persistence` option fixes that from the browser\nside: on reload it repaints the transcript, brings back a pending interrupt, and\nrejoins a run that was mid-stream.\n\nYou need this whether or not you have a server:\n\n- **The browser owns the chat** (SPA, offline-first, no server store). Pass a\n  storage adapter and it holds the full transcript, restored on reload with no\n  network.\n- **The server owns the chat** (you use [Chat persistence](./chat-persistence)).\n  Set `persistence: true` and the client caches nothing: on reload it hydrates\n  the thread from the server by its `threadId`, painting the conversation and\n  rejoining any run still streaming. That is the server-authoritative mode below.\n\n## Turn it on\n\nPass a storage adapter as `persistence` and give the chat a stable `threadId` so\na reload finds the same record:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  localStoragePersistence,\n  useChat,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n  })\n  // ...render messages, call sendMessage(text)\n}\n```\n\n`localStoragePersistence()` needs no type argument and no codec: it defaults to\nthe chat record shape and a JSON codec. That is the whole opt-in.\n\nThe `threadId` is doing the real work here: it is the key the record is written\nunder and looked up by, so a fresh id per mount restores nothing. Derive it from\nyour own domain (a conversation id, a route param). [Id map](./id-map) covers how\nto pick one and how it differs from the `runId` the hook reports.\n\n## What a reload restores\n\nThe client stores one record per `threadId`, the transcript plus a small resume\npointer. On the next load `useChat` reads it and:\n\n- **Repaints the transcript** from storage with no network. Sync adapters\n  (`localStorage` / `sessionStorage`) hydrate during construction. IndexedDB\n  hydrates asynchronously after the database opens. Until then, `isHydrating`\n  is `true`, so you can show a loading state instead of an empty chat.\n- **Rehydrates a pending interrupt**, so an approval prompt comes back exactly as\n  it was.\n- **Rejoins an in-flight run**, if a reply was still streaming when the page\n  reloaded, so it finishes in place instead of freezing half-done. This one needs\n  a durability-backed connection (a route that records the stream and exposes a\n  replay handler); see [Resumable streams](../resumable-streams/overview).\n\nReplay rebuilds reasoning, tool activity, and text from the durable log, including runs that emit reasoning before their first tool or text event. The completed activity remains in the transcript sent with the next message.\n\n### AG-UI activity rows\n\nAG-UI activity events show as `role: 'activity'` rows in `messages`.\n\n- A client storage adapter keeps each row with the same `id` and content.\n- `persistence: true` restores the rows from the server only when the server\n  has an `activities` store. See\n  [AG-UI activity rows on reload](./chat-persistence#ag-ui-activity-rows-on-reload).\n\nThe next `sendMessage` does not send activity rows as model input.\n\n### Handle restored client tools\n\nA live client tool runs automatically when its call arrives from the stream.\nHydration restores its pending execution but does not run the browser code\nagain, because that work may not be safe to repeat. The execution remains an\ninternal interrupt and does not appear in `interrupts`.\n\nUse `onInterruptStateChange` to distinguish restored interrupt state from live\nupdates. Leaving a restored batch pending is the default. This example cancels\nevery restored batch instead:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  localStoragePersistence,\n  useChat,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const [restoredBatch, setRestoredBatch] = useState(false)\n  const { cancelInterrupts } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n    onInterruptStateChange(_state, { source }) {\n      setRestoredBatch(source === 'hydrate')\n    },\n  })\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (restoredBatch) cancelInterrupts()\n  }, [cancelInterrupts, restoredBatch])\n\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n`source` is `hydrate` for state restored from an initial resume snapshot, a\nclient storage adapter, or server hydration. It is `live` for streamed and\nclient-initiated changes. `cancelInterrupts()` cancels the complete internal\nbatch, including visible approvals and hidden client-tool executions; it does\nnot selectively cancel one kind of interrupt.\n\n## Choose a mode\n\n`persistence` takes a storage adapter or a boolean:\n\n- an **adapter** (`persistence: localStoragePersistence()`) is client-authoritative.\n- **`true`** is server-authoritative.\n- **`false`** (or omitted) is off: messages live in memory only and a reload starts empty.\n\nThe generation hooks take the same option, boolean only. See\n[Generation persistence](./generation-persistence).\n\n### An adapter: client-authoritative\n\nPass the adapter directly, `persistence: localStoragePersistence()`. The\ntranscript and the resume pointer both live in the browser. The client owns the\nhistory; the server, if any, mirrors it. Best when the browser is the source of\ntruth: single-page apps, offline-first, one device, small to moderate\nconversations.\n\n### `true`: server-authoritative\n\nPass `persistence: true`. The client stores nothing, no transcript and no resume\npointer. On mount `useChat` hydrates the thread from the server by its\n`threadId`: it paints the stored transcript and, if a run is still generating,\ntails it to completion. `history: { pageSize }` paints the newest window on\nhydrate. Best when transcripts are large (localStorage is\nsynchronous and quota-bound), when the same conversation must open on another\ndevice, or when you simply do not want message content in the browser.\n\nYou do not fetch or seed the transcript yourself. A reload and the same thread\nopened on another device follow the identical path, because the thread id is the\nstable key and the server resolves everything from it. No loader, no\n`initialMessages`, no extra props. It needs a connection with a `hydrate` handler\n(every built-in connection has one) and the server `GET` endpoint below.\n\n**Client**: a connection, a stable `threadId`, and `persistence: true`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nfunction Chat({ threadId }: { threadId: string }) {\n  const {\n    messages,\n    isHydrating,\n    hasOlderMessages,\n    loadOlderMessages,\n    sendMessage,\n  } = useChat({\n    threadId,\n    connection,\n    persistence: true,\n    history: { pageSize: 50 },\n  })\n  if (isHydrating) return <p>Loading conversation...</p>\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {hasOlderMessages ? (\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          onClick={() => {\n            void loadOlderMessages().catch(() => {\n              // Show a retry. Painted messages stay.\n            })\n          }}\n        >\n          Load older\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      {messages.map((m) => (\n        <div key={m.id}>{m.role}</div>\n      ))}\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => void sendMessage('hi')}>\n        Send\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nCall `loadOlderMessages()` from your scroll handler. The library does not watch\nthe scrollbar.\n\n- `isHydrating` is `true` from the first render until the transcript is in\n  place. If a run is still generating, `isLoading` is already `true` when\n  `isHydrating` turns `false`. If the load fails, `isHydrating` turns `false`\n  and `error` is set.\n- `hasOlderMessages` follows `page.truncated` on the last hydrate or older-page\n  response.\n- Without `history`, hydrate loads the full thread.\n- `history` is only valid with `persistence: true`.\n- With `history.pageSize`, send posts only the new turn. Reload posts the last\n  user (the old assistant is already gone locally). Resume posts from that\n  user through the painted assistant so the stored tool-call is not dropped.\n- If `loadOlderMessages()` fails, the promise rejects and painted messages\n  stay. `hasOlderMessages` stays true. Catch the rejection in your UI.\n\n**Server**: one `GET` endpoint next to your chat `POST`. Replay the durability\nlog when the request carries a resume cursor, otherwise return the stored\nconversation with `reconstructChat`:\n\n```ts\nimport { memoryStream, resumeServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Response | Promise<Response> {\n  const durability = memoryStream(request)\n  // A reconnecting client carries a resume cursor (Last-Event-ID / ?offset and\n  // X-Run-Id / ?runId). Replay the log so the run finishes in place.\n  if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n    return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n  }\n  // Otherwise return the stored transcript plus a cursor to any in-flight run.\n  // Guard access in multi-user apps (see authorize in Chat persistence).\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request)\n}\n```\n\n`reconstructChat` returns `{ messages, activeRun }`: the transcript as UI\nmessages, and `activeRun` when a run is still generating for the thread. With a\nvalid `limit` query param, the body also has `page: { truncated, cursor }`.\n`reconstructChat` reads `limit` and `before` from the query.\n\nThe client calls this endpoint on mount and, when `activeRun` is set, tails the\nrun through the replay branch above. You never handle a run id, and a second\ndevice resumes the live run the same way the original tab does. See\n[Chat persistence](./chat-persistence).\n\n### Show how long each turn took\n\nA live turn can time itself on the client. After a reload, that time is gone. Pass `includeRuns: true` to get it back from the server:\n\n```ts\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request, { includeRuns: true })\n}\n```\n\nEach assistant message of a finished run then has the run's timings, in epoch ms, on `metadata.tanstack.run`:\n\n```tsx\nimport type { UIMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction TurnDuration({ message }: { message: UIMessage }) {\n  const run = message.metadata?.tanstack?.run\n  if (!run?.finishedAt) return null\n  const seconds = Math.round((run.finishedAt - run.startedAt) / 1000)\n  return <span>Worked for {seconds}s</span>\n}\n```\n\nThe response also has a top-level `runs` list with `runId`, `status`, `startedAt`, and `finishedAt` for each finished run. The timings need a `runs` store that implements `listByThread`, and messages that were saved by `withPersistence` with this version or later.\n\n| Mode | Caches on client | Authoritative history | Reach for it when |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `persistence: store` | transcript + resume pointer | client | SPA / offline, one device, small to moderate history |\n| `persistence: true` | nothing | server | large histories, multi-device, no transcripts in the browser |\n\n## Choose a storage backend\n\nThree adapters ship from `@tanstack/ai-client`, re-exported from every framework\npackage. All share the same shape; they differ in lifetime and encoding.\n\n| Adapter | Lifetime | Notes | Reach for it when |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `localStoragePersistence` | across reloads and browser restarts | synchronous, ~5MB quota, JSON codec | the default: persist a conversation for next time |\n| `sessionStoragePersistence` | one tab, cleared when it closes | same shape as localStorage | a conversation that should not outlive the tab |\n| `indexedDBPersistence` | across reloads and restarts | async, structured clone (a `Date` round-trips exactly), room for large data | big transcripts, or values a JSON codec would mangle |\n\n```tsx\nimport { indexedDBPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst persistence = indexedDBPersistence()\n```\n\nEach throws only lazily, per operation, when its backing store is missing (for\nexample during server-side rendering), so constructing one on the server is safe.\n\n### Writing your own\n\nAny object with `getItem` / `setItem` / `removeItem` works. The record is one\n`{ messages, resume? }` blob per chat id (the transcript plus the pointer that\nlets a reload rejoin an in-flight run), so `setItem` receives that whole record,\nnot a bare message array:\n\n```ts\nimport type {\n  ChatClientPersistence,\n  ChatPersistedState,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nfunction isPersistedState(value: unknown): value is ChatPersistedState {\n  return (\n    typeof value === 'object' &&\n    value !== null &&\n    'messages' in value &&\n    Array.isArray(value.messages)\n  )\n}\n\nconst persistence: ChatClientPersistence = {\n  getItem(id) {\n    const raw = localStorage.getItem(id)\n    if (raw === null) return null\n    const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(raw)\n    // A bare array is the legacy messages-only format, still accepted.\n    if (Array.isArray(parsed)) return { messages: parsed }\n    return isPersistedState(parsed) ? parsed : null\n  },\n  setItem(id, state) {\n    localStorage.setItem(id, JSON.stringify(state))\n  },\n  removeItem(id) {\n    localStorage.removeItem(id)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nReads are best-effort: a `getItem` that throws or returns `null` is treated as\n\"nothing stored\", so an adapter that parses the wrong shape fails **silently**:\nthe conversation just does not come back. Round-trip your adapter once against a\nreal reload before shipping it.\n\n## Client and server are independent\n\nClient persistence restores what one browser rendered. Server persistence\n([Chat persistence](./chat-persistence)) keeps the authoritative copy for every\nuser and survives a server restart. They compose: for the combination we\nrecommend for most apps, and why, see the\n[Persistence overview](./overview#what-we-recommend).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Client Persistence\nid: client-persistence\n---\n\nA `ChatClient` (and every framework `useChat` / `createChat`) keeps messages in\nmemory, so a reload or a crashed tab loses the whole conversation and any reply\nthat was still streaming. The `persistence` option fixes that from the browser\nside: on reload it repaints the transcript, brings back a pending interrupt, and\nrejoins a run that was mid-stream.\n\nYou need this whether or not you have a server:\n\n- **The browser owns the chat** (SPA, offline-first, no server store). Pass a\n  storage adapter and it holds the full transcript, restored on reload with no\n  network.\n- **The server owns the chat** (you use [Chat persistence](./chat-persistence)).\n  Set `persistence: true` and the client caches nothing: on reload it hydrates\n  the thread from the server by its `threadId`, painting the conversation and\n  rejoining any run still streaming. That is the server-authoritative mode below.\n\n## Turn it on\n\nPass a storage adapter as `persistence` and give the chat a stable `threadId` so\na reload finds the same record:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  localStoragePersistence,\n  useChat,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n  })\n  // ...render messages, call sendMessage(text)\n}\n```\n\n`localStoragePersistence()` needs no type argument and no codec: it defaults to\nthe chat record shape and a JSON codec. That is the whole opt-in.\n\nThe `threadId` is doing the real work here: it is the key the record is written\nunder and looked up by, so a fresh id per mount restores nothing. Derive it from\nyour own domain (a conversation id, a route param). [Id map](./id-map) covers how\nto pick one and how it differs from the `runId` the hook reports.\n\n## What a reload restores\n\nThe client stores one record per `threadId`, the transcript plus a small resume\npointer. On the next load `useChat` reads it and:\n\n- **Repaints the transcript** from storage with no network. Sync adapters\n  (`localStorage` / `sessionStorage`) hydrate during construction. IndexedDB\n  hydrates asynchronously after the database opens. Until then, `isHydrating`\n  is `true`, so you can show a loading state instead of an empty chat.\n- **Rehydrates a pending interrupt**, so an approval prompt comes back exactly as\n  it was.\n- **Rejoins an in-flight run**, if a reply was still streaming when the page\n  reloaded, so it finishes in place instead of freezing half-done. This one needs\n  a durability-backed connection (a route that records the stream and exposes a\n  replay handler); see [Resumable streams](../resumable-streams/overview).\n\nReplay rebuilds reasoning, tool activity, and text from the durable log, including runs that emit reasoning before their first tool or text event. The completed activity remains in the transcript sent with the next message.\n\n### AG-UI activity rows\n\nAG-UI activity events show as `role: 'activity'` rows in `messages`.\n\n- A client storage adapter keeps each row with the same `id` and content.\n- `persistence: true` restores the rows from the server only when the server\n  has an `activities` store. See\n  [AG-UI activity rows on reload](./chat-persistence#ag-ui-activity-rows-on-reload).\n\nThe next `sendMessage` does not send activity rows as model input.\n\n### Handle restored client tools\n\nA live client tool runs automatically when its call arrives from the stream.\nHydration restores its pending execution but does not run the browser code\nagain, because that work may not be safe to repeat. The execution remains an\ninternal interrupt and does not appear in `interrupts`.\n\nUse `onInterruptStateChange` to distinguish restored interrupt state from live\nupdates. Leaving a restored batch pending is the default. This example cancels\nevery restored batch instead:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  localStoragePersistence,\n  useChat,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const [restoredBatch, setRestoredBatch] = useState(false)\n  const { cancelInterrupts } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n    onInterruptStateChange(_state, { source }) {\n      setRestoredBatch(source === 'hydrate')\n    },\n  })\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (restoredBatch) cancelInterrupts()\n  }, [cancelInterrupts, restoredBatch])\n\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n`source` is `hydrate` for state restored from an initial resume snapshot, a\nclient storage adapter, or server hydration. It is `live` for streamed and\nclient-initiated changes. `cancelInterrupts()` cancels the complete internal\nbatch, including visible approvals and hidden client-tool executions; it does\nnot selectively cancel one kind of interrupt.\n\n## Choose a mode\n\n`persistence` takes a storage adapter or a boolean:\n\n- an **adapter** (`persistence: localStoragePersistence()`) is client-authoritative.\n- **`true`** is server-authoritative.\n- **`false`** (or omitted) is off: messages live in memory only and a reload starts empty.\n\nThe generation hooks take the same option, boolean only. See\n[Generation persistence](./generation-persistence).\n\n### An adapter: client-authoritative\n\nPass the adapter directly, `persistence: localStoragePersistence()`. The\ntranscript and the resume pointer both live in the browser. The client owns the\nhistory; the server, if any, mirrors it. Best when the browser is the source of\ntruth: single-page apps, offline-first, one device, small to moderate\nconversations.\n\n### `true`: server-authoritative\n\nPass `persistence: true`. The client stores nothing, no transcript and no resume\npointer. On mount `useChat` hydrates the thread from the server by its\n`threadId`: it paints the stored transcript and, if a run is still generating,\ntails it to completion. `history: { pageSize }` paints the newest window on\nhydrate. Best when transcripts are large (localStorage is\nsynchronous and quota-bound), when the same conversation must open on another\ndevice, or when you simply do not want message content in the browser.\n\nYou do not fetch or seed the transcript yourself. A reload and the same thread\nopened on another device follow the identical path, because the thread id is the\nstable key and the server resolves everything from it. No loader, no\n`initialMessages`, no extra props. It needs a connection with a `hydrate` handler\n(every built-in connection has one) and the server `GET` endpoint below.\n\n**Client**: a connection, a stable `threadId`, and `persistence: true`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nfunction Chat({ threadId }: { threadId: string }) {\n  const {\n    messages,\n    isHydrating,\n    hasOlderMessages,\n    loadOlderMessages,\n    sendMessage,\n  } = useChat({\n    threadId,\n    connection,\n    persistence: true,\n    history: { pageSize: 50 },\n  })\n  if (isHydrating) return <p>Loading conversation...</p>\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {hasOlderMessages ? (\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          onClick={() => {\n            void loadOlderMessages().catch(() => {\n              // Show a retry. Painted messages stay.\n            })\n          }}\n        >\n          Load older\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      {messages.map((m) => (\n        <div key={m.id}>{m.role}</div>\n      ))}\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => void sendMessage('hi')}>\n        Send\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nCall `loadOlderMessages()` from your scroll handler. The library does not watch\nthe scrollbar.\n\n- `isHydrating` is `true` from the first render until the transcript is in\n  place. If a run is still generating, `isLoading` is already `true` when\n  `isHydrating` turns `false`. If the load fails, `isHydrating` turns `false`\n  and `error` is set.\n- `hasOlderMessages` follows `page.truncated` on the last hydrate or older-page\n  response.\n- Without `history`, hydrate loads the full thread.\n- `history` is only valid with `persistence: true`.\n- With `history.pageSize`, send posts only the new turn. Reload posts the last\n  user (the old assistant is already gone locally). Resume posts from that\n  user through the painted assistant so the stored tool-call is not dropped.\n- If `loadOlderMessages()` fails, the promise rejects and painted messages\n  stay. `hasOlderMessages` stays true. Catch the rejection in your UI.\n\n**Server**: one `GET` endpoint next to your chat `POST`. Replay the durability\nlog when the request carries a resume cursor, otherwise return the stored\nconversation with `reconstructChat`:\n\n```ts\nimport { memoryStream, resumeServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Response | Promise<Response> {\n  const durability = memoryStream(request)\n  // A reconnecting client carries a resume cursor (Last-Event-ID / ?offset and\n  // X-Run-Id / ?runId). Replay the log so the run finishes in place.\n  if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n    return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n  }\n  // Otherwise return the stored transcript plus a cursor to any in-flight run.\n  // Guard access in multi-user apps (see authorize in Chat persistence).\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request)\n}\n```\n\n`reconstructChat` returns `{ messages, activeRun }`: the transcript as UI\nmessages, and `activeRun` when a run is still generating for the thread. With a\nvalid `limit` query param, the body also has `page: { truncated, cursor }`.\n`reconstructChat` reads `limit` and `before` from the query.\n\nThe client calls this endpoint on mount and, when `activeRun` is set, tails the\nrun through the replay branch above. You never handle a run id, and a second\ndevice resumes the live run the same way the original tab does. See\n[Chat persistence](./chat-persistence).\n\n### Show how long each turn took\n\nA live turn can time itself on the client. After a reload, that time is gone. Pass `includeRuns: true` to get it back from the server:\n\n```ts\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request, { includeRuns: true })\n}\n```\n\nEach assistant message of a finished run then has the run's timings, in epoch ms, on `metadata.tanstack.run`:\n\n```tsx\nimport type { UIMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction TurnDuration({ message }: { message: UIMessage }) {\n  const run = message.metadata?.tanstack?.run\n  if (!run?.finishedAt) return null\n  const seconds = Math.round((run.finishedAt - run.startedAt) / 1000)\n  return <span>Worked for {seconds}s</span>\n}\n```\n\nThe response also has a top-level `runs` list with `runId`, `status`, `startedAt`, and `finishedAt` for each finished run. The timings need a `runs` store that implements `listByThread`, and messages that were saved by `withPersistence` with this version or later.\n\n| Mode | Caches on client | Authoritative history | Reach for it when |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `persistence: store` | transcript + resume pointer | client | SPA / offline, one device, small to moderate history |\n| `persistence: true` | nothing | server | large histories, multi-device, no transcripts in the browser |\n\n## Choose a storage backend\n\nThree adapters ship from `@tanstack/ai-client`, re-exported from every framework\npackage. All share the same shape; they differ in lifetime and encoding.\n\n| Adapter | Lifetime | Notes | Reach for it when |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `localStoragePersistence` | across reloads and browser restarts | synchronous, ~5MB quota, JSON codec | the default: persist a conversation for next time |\n| `sessionStoragePersistence` | one tab, cleared when it closes | same shape as localStorage | a conversation that should not outlive the tab |\n| `indexedDBPersistence` | across reloads and restarts | async, structured clone (a `Date` round-trips exactly), room for large data | big transcripts, or values a JSON codec would mangle |\n\n```tsx\nimport { indexedDBPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst persistence = indexedDBPersistence()\n```\n\nEach throws only lazily, per operation, when its backing store is missing (for\nexample during server-side rendering), so constructing one on the server is safe.\n\n### Writing your own\n\nAny object with `getItem` / `setItem` / `removeItem` works. The record is one\n`{ messages, resume? }` blob per chat id (the transcript plus the pointer that\nlets a reload rejoin an in-flight run), so `setItem` receives that whole record,\nnot a bare message array:\n\n```ts\nimport type {\n  ChatClientPersistence,\n  ChatPersistedState,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nfunction isPersistedState(value: unknown): value is ChatPersistedState {\n  return (\n    typeof value === 'object' &&\n    value !== null &&\n    'messages' in value &&\n    Array.isArray(value.messages)\n  )\n}\n\nconst persistence: ChatClientPersistence = {\n  getItem(id) {\n    const raw = localStorage.getItem(id)\n    if (raw === null) return null\n    const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(raw)\n    // A bare array is the legacy messages-only format, still accepted.\n    if (Array.isArray(parsed)) return { messages: parsed }\n    return isPersistedState(parsed) ? parsed : null\n  },\n  setItem(id, state) {\n    localStorage.setItem(id, JSON.stringify(state))\n  },\n  removeItem(id) {\n    localStorage.removeItem(id)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nReads are best-effort: a `getItem` that throws or returns `null` is treated as\n\"nothing stored\", so an adapter that parses the wrong shape fails **silently**:\nthe conversation just does not come back. Round-trip your adapter once against a\nreal reload before shipping it.\n\n## Client and server are independent\n\nClient persistence restores what one browser rendered. Server persistence\n([Chat persistence](./chat-persistence)) keeps the authoritative copy for every\nuser and survives a server restart. They compose: for the combination we\nrecommend for most apps, and why, see the\n[Persistence overview](./overview#what-we-recommend).\n"}
